==== Temporary OpenWrt ====

  - Download the latest OpenWrt initramfs-kernel
    - [[https://downloads.openwrt.org/releases/|Releases]] -> Latest stable version -> targets -> lantiq -> xway -> Download arcadyan_arv752dpw-initramfs-kernel.bin
    - If the latest version doesn't work, use this working version [[https://downloads.openwrt.org/releases/22.03.6/targets/lantiq/xway/openwrt-22.03.6-lantiq-xway-arcadyan_arv752dpw-initramfs-kernel.bin]]
  - Get the size of the initramfs-kernel OpenWrt image by typing in your linux terminal <code>printf "%x\n" `stat -c "%s" "<initramfs-kernel bin file>"`</code> **Replace <initramfs-kernel bin file>**\\ The result is needed later
  - Connect to the serial header ([[arv752dpw#open_up_and_connect_cable|Open up and connect cable]])
  - Upload the initramfs-kernel image to RAM
    - First quick way: xmodem
      - Calculate crc32 checksum of the OpenWrt initramfs-kernel image by typing <code>crc32 <initramfs-kernel bin file></code> **Replace <initramfs-kernel bin file>**\\ Maybe requires additional package e.g. for Ubuntu install package ''libarchive-zip-perl''
      - Open a serial console by typing <code>screen /dev/ttyUSB0 115200</code>
      - Start the xmodem upload mode of your device by typing <code>loadx</code>
      - Close your serial connection by pressing the key combination in the terminal <code>[CTRL] + [A] then [K] then [Y] to confirm exit</code>
      - Upload the OpenWrt initramfs-kernel image from your local computer to the RAM of the device by typing <code>sx <initramfs-kernel bin file> </dev/ttyUSB0 >/dev/ttyUSB0</code> **Replace <initramfs-kernel bin file>**\\ Maybe requires additional package e.g. for Ubuntu install package ''lrzsz''
      - After the transfer is complete, open your serial connection again by typing <code>screen /dev/ttyUSB0 115200</code>
      - Open the menu again by hitting <code>[ENTER]</code>
    - Second quick Way: tftp
      - Connect ''LAN 1'' of device with your computer
        - You can also use a USB Ethernet adapter
      - Download a tftp server, e.g. Tftpd64 on Windows ([[:docs:guide-user:troubleshooting:tftpserver#setting_up_tftp_server|General explanation]])
        - For Tftpd64: Browse to the folder with the image in it
      - Open a serial console by typing <code>screen /dev/ttyUSB0 115200</code>
      - Get the client IP and server IP by typing <code>printenv</code> <code>ARV752DPW22 # printenv
